# The sdist is built from the WORKING TREE, where the research material and the internal documents
# sit beside pyproject.toml — gitignored, so a clean checkout does not have them, and present on
# every machine that actually cuts a release. Nothing below is currently reached by setuptools'
# defaults; these lines exist so that a later `graft`/`include` cannot sweep them in by accident.
# `tests/test_distribution.py` fails if any of it reaches an artifact, and was shown to fail on a
# planted leak.
# The sdist is a source distribution: a packager or a `pip download` user expects the changelog and
# the build tooling the tests import. Only pruning meant it shipped `tests/` that could not run.
include CHANGELOG.md SECURITY.md
recursive-include packaging *.py *.toml

prune experiments
prune runs
prune data
prune docs/notes
prune .claude
exclude E3_*.md
exclude ROADMAP_INTERNAL.md
exclude *.db
